Z||000019||ChopTop||08-24-2001||02:56 PM||||1FST2M6, Wheels look great, really adds an exotic touch to your car. You mentioned you didn't feel 18s looked right on the front along with the 18s on the rear.  Could you please explain why you feel that way?  I've gone back and forth on that issue, meaning should I go with the same wheel all around or go with the one inch smaller wheel on the front.  As of right now I'd want to stay with one size, but am interested in your opinion.  Thanks in advance.||||reg||1
Z||000020||1FST2M6||08-24-2001||03:09 PM||||if i could find an 18x7 with a 40mm offset they woud be ok. but the 42-45 are the way most wheels are now they all stick out past the wheel well. there is a guy in the Ga. Fieros club with 4 18.. the front of his car looks cocked up and out of alignment. i know it's not he's got a 3.4tdc and it's a killer car but just doesnt' fit. if you got a hold of Dymag, Fikse, HRE, Forge Line, Racing Hart or one of the other custom wheel manufacturers i'm sure you can have them cut to fit. they would look ok if you could push the wheel in 1/2". it just pokes out of the wheel well. well the ones i've seen do. and 19s on the back.. BEEN there too. it's a lesson in fabrication and preperation H. unless you can get a 19x7.5-45mm an 8" won't work it hits the strut you cut the spring purch and your in carrera coil over territory. and your tire still rubs the strut hosing.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> and having custom made springs I was NOT gunna ditch the springs for a mis matched set of coil over springs. just to ad spacers, longer studs and coil overs just to have 19s. <P>Just my $.02 <P><BR>oh Cost um under $2k. and i got them at the Wheel Source <A HREF="http://www.wheel1.com" TARGET=_blank>www.wheel1.com</A>  a sales rep/ fellow Solo driver Doug Greenup was at the shop on a dyno day (Grassroots Motorsports magazine) <BR>they sell Koni too.. anyone in for a group buy?<BR> <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstmeat1.jpg">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 08-24-2001).]||||reg||1
